WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.434
-Thanks for having me.
It's been a while.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.803
-It's been a while.
-It has.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.305
-How old is baby now?
-Baby is 3 1/2.

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:08.474
-Wow! Is that right?
-Baby's a toddler.

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:10.376
Baby's not a baby.
-Baby's not a baby anymore.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:12.178
-Yeah, she's huge.
-3 1/2.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:15.081
-3 1/2.
-Are you into "Paw Patrol"?

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.550
-Oh.
-I'm sorry, yeah.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.985
-Yeah.
-Are you into all those shows?

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:21.754
-Ah, "Paw Patrol."
Yeah, no, we are.

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:25.057
We're really, really deep, deep,
deep into "Paw Patrol."

00:00:25.057 --> 00:00:26.258
-Have you done "Dora"?

00:00:26.258 --> 00:00:28.895
-Yeah, but it's like
toddler crack, isn't it?

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:30.663
-No, yeah, no.
-I mean, which is kind of

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.632
a good thing, because,
you know, you go, "Okay."

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.933
It's been Saturday night,
and maybe you've had

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.635
a couple of more glasses of wine
than you should have,

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.170
and Sunday morning,
"Paw Patrol"...

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.671
-...is the best thing
that ever existed

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.573
in the history of the world.
-Absolutely amazing.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.208
-Yes, exactly.
Thank you, "Paw Patrol."

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:47.146
-But if you don't have
the hangover, it's just...

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.714
So we don't just have, like --

00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:50.983
'Cause we have
to act it out, as well.

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:52.318
-Oh, I didn't know that.

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.453
-Yeah, yeah, constantly,
'cause it's the bathtime thing.

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:56.589
We have bath toys,
"Paw Patrol" is in the bath.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.491
I mean, it's everywhere,
but it's in the bath.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.893
And she'll
only let me be Rubble.

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:03.262
And, okay, the parents --
parents in the audience

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:05.464
would understand this,
but Rubble's rubbish.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.566
-Oh, no, come on, now!
No, come on.

00:01:07.566 --> 00:01:10.270
-I want to be Skye!
She has to be Skye.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.005
You know, but she will only
let me be Rubble.

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:13.339
And then,
she tells me off about it.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:16.509
"No, don't do that.
No, he doesn't talk like that."

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.278
I'm like,
"I get paid for this."

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:20.213
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:23.616
-"Mommy is a professional actor!
Hello!"

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:24.817
-Mommy knows what she's doing.

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.785
-"This is the way
Rubble talks from now on."

00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:28.621
-She won't have it.
-Oh, gosh.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.190
Oh, get used to that.
My kids are over the --

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.092
I mean, they're super
into "Paw Patrol" now,

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:35.261
but I'm into it now.
-Are you?

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.797
-Yeah, I'm like into the plot
lines and all the stuff, yeah.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:39.632
-Yeah, it's deep.
It's really deep.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.468
-It's really, really deep.
Well, congrats on baby,

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:45.171
and I know you're married
and your husband is a musician.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.506
-Yes.
-Are you musical?

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:47.974
-No.
-You're not?

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.342
-No, no.
-I always thought you were.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.344
-No, I mean, I played the flute
when I was at school.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.711
-Hey, there you go.
-Yeah, there you go, thanks.

00:01:52.711 --> 00:01:54.580
I mean, I probably
can't anymore, but, no, no.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:57.483
-No musical talent at all?
No hidden talent?

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:59.986
-No. Oh, no, what?
Oh, yes, there is one.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.354
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.655
-There might be one, maybe?

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.691
-There's a very special one,
yes.

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:08.695
-I heard that maybe one.
-Yeah, I can play my teeth.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:09.895
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.895 --> 00:02:11.664
-Now how did you
come up with this?

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.032
How did you know
that you had this talent?

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:16.436
-Well, there was a boy at school
when I was about 7 or 8,

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:18.638
and he went
on a talent show on TV,

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.206
so he was, like,
the coolest person ever,

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.942
and he played his teeth,
so everybody at my school

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.477
was like, "Wow, that's cool."

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:26.078
So everybody from that school,
I think,

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:28.481
can probably play their teeth.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.416
So, obsessively
playing their teeth.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.117
-I mean, I don't know.
I mean, the audience

00:02:32.117 --> 00:02:34.220
might not want to hear
a little sample --

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.921
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:35.921 --> 00:02:37.256
Come on!

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:39.192
We would love it if you could
just give us a taste.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.628
We'll be very quiet.
-Okay. I mean, what do you want?

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:43.062
-All right,
maybe just give me a classic.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.363
-Okay.
I mean, classic is

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:45.764
"Raindrops Keep Falling
on Your Head,"

00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:47.366
'cause I think that's what
he played on the talent show.

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:50.035
So, like,
that's what I first learned.

00:02:50.035 --> 00:02:53.839
Would you like that?
-I would love that.

00:02:53.839 --> 00:03:08.788
♪♪

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:11.123
Oh, my God!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:13.592
You even did
"Nothing's bothering me."

00:03:13.592 --> 00:03:14.627
-Thanks.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.262
You even did
"Nothing's bothering me."

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.764
-Of course.
-That is musical talent!

00:03:18.764 --> 00:03:20.098
That's fantastic.

00:03:20.098 --> 00:03:22.901
Could you do like a newer song,
like a more modern song?

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:25.037
-Yeah, I mean, yeah.
What would you like?

00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:28.507
I can do anything you like.
What would you like?

00:03:28.507 --> 00:03:30.276
-Could you do "Despacito"?

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.577
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:33.412
-Sure.
Uh, a moment..

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:35.481
[ Humming ]
Okay.

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:45.491
♪♪

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.793
-Oh, my God!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:50.696
Should write an album!
-Thank you.

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:52.364
-That's a record album!
-Yes!

00:03:52.364 --> 00:03:54.900
-That's fantastic!
That's an album right there.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.302
I would totally buy that.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.204
-I can't believe my husband
hasn't put me in a band yet.

00:03:58.204 --> 00:03:59.939
-I mean, what is he thinking?
Yeah, please.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.809
-Yeah, I know.
-I read something, also,

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.810
about you that --
it said that you only

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.580
watch your movies once, if that.
-Yeah, if that.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.947
Yes, yeah.
-Why?

00:04:08.947 --> 00:04:11.250
Just 'cause you don't
want to watch yourself?

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.885
I mean, you're great.
-Thank you.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.887
No, yeah, I don't know.
It's just wei-- It's weird.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.389
It's like
hearing your own voice.

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.956
It's like, you know --
I don't know.

00:04:17.956 --> 00:04:19.358
And I only see the bad bits,
so I'm like,

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:22.061
"Oh. Why did I do that?"
-So, when you see this photo,

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.996
don't you go,
"I was in 'Love Actually.'

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:26.899
This is a great --
I have to watch this movie."

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.669
-Do you know what the only thing
that I really remember

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:31.871
from doing "Love Actually" --
I was 17 --

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:37.076
and this -- this --
I got the biggest zit of my life

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:38.544
when we were
shooting this scene.

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:39.645
And this scene was like --

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:40.913
It's the important one,
isn't it?

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.214
-This is where
you're watching the wedding.

00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:44.784
-Yeah, so it was literally --
it was like another head

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:46.052
growing out of my head.

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:47.720
And I was only in the film --
It's a small part.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.455
I was only on it for two weeks,
and, like, the chances

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.224
of getting this extra head...

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:52.725
And so they went in,
and they tried to cover it,

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:53.892
and they tried to light it,
and there was nothing

00:04:53.892 --> 00:04:55.128
they could do,
so the hat went on.

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:56.395
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:57.964
-Is that the reason
why you're wearing the hat?

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:59.198
-Yeah, that's the reason
for the hat.

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:00.566
-Wow! I thought
it was just a fashion choice.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:02.468
-I mean, it was lucky
it wasn't anywhere else, though,

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:04.337
'cause I don't know
what we would've done.

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:05.938
-You're wearing a scarf
around your whole head.

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:07.907
Oh, my gosh.
That's good triv.

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:09.141
-Yeah.
-I love that.

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:10.809
Every time I watch it now,
I'll think of that.

00:05:10.809 --> 00:05:13.078
And I'll watch it every year.
Trust me, I love it.

00:05:13.078 --> 00:05:14.447
Let's talk about
"The Aftermath."

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.749
-Yes.
-What a great film.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.918
A cool choice of a film,
I would say.

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:21.821
'Cause I've seen "War Room"
and stuff like that,

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:23.656
but this deals
with a different subject.

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.391
-Yeah, it does.
It sort of deals with

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:28.627
the direct aftermath
of World War II and kind of --

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:31.630
I think it asks the questions
about how do you get over

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:34.166
a catastrophic conflict
like that

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:36.502
and how do you rebuild yourself,
personally,

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.604
but, also, how do nations
rebuild themselves?

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:39.872
So it's kind of
a story about that.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:42.475
So, it's a tragedy.
It's also a love triangle,

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:46.245
but it's kind of, I think,
a story of redemption and hope.

